  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1231 PM MST Tue Nov 3 2026\n\nCurrently there is weak high pressure over our area with clouds\nstarting to move over our area in southwest flow from an upper \nlevel low located currently over northern California.\n\nModels show the low over northern California weakening and\nmoving over central Utah giving our southern areas a slight\nchance of showers later Wednesday. Little, if any, precipitation\nis currently expected. Temperatures Wednesday warm slightly \ncompared to Tuesday with highs in the mid 40s to mid 50s. \n\nBy Thursday, an upper level low will move over northern Idaho. \nExpect slightly breezy winds and just a slight chance of \nprecipitation, especially across the Wyoming border. Temperatures \ndrop slightly Thursday with temperatures in the low 40s to low \n50s. \n\nExpect patchy fog Wednesday morning and, especially, Thursday \nand Friday mornings, particularly near water sources. \n\nExpect a warm up Friday into Saturday under high pressure. Look\nfor Saturday high temperatures in the low 50s and low 60s.",
